<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use" description="Read the terms governing your use of MushroomScope educational content."><div class="shell py-8"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Terms of Use'}]} /></div><article class="shell max-w-4xl py-12"><h1 class="font-serif text-5xl">Terms of Use</h1><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: July 31, 2026</p><div class="prose mt-8"><h2>Educational information</h2><p>MushroomScope provides general educational information. It is not a substitute for professional medical advice, local expert identification, or emergency guidance.</p><h2>Wild mushroom safety</h2><p>Never consume a wild mushroom based only on a website, photograph, automated tool, or unverified opinion. Some poisonous species closely resemble edible species.</p><h2>Accuracy and availability</h2><p>We work to improve our content but cannot guarantee that every page is complete, current, or applicable to your location.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
